      "content": "Those symptoms could indicate a transient ischemic attack (TIA), which is often called a \"mini-stroke.\" Because TIAs are a critical warning sign of a potential future stroke, you should seek immediate emergency medical attention even though you feel fine now. Do not wait for home results or assume it was nothing, as it is always safer to get evaluated by a doctor right away. Please contact emergency services or go to the nearest ER immediately.",
